From 47805720787984d3e78ea3b2d0d2123f3eb8070b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: belikh <io@jupiter.au>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:24:42 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the mips64 arch layer for the SGI Indy (IP24)

A MIPS R4400 n32 big-endian kernel with 32-bit addresses, entered directly
from the SGI PROM over `boot -f bootp()redox` (ECOFF, no bootloader).

- targets/mips64-unknown-kernel.json, linkers/mips64.ld: image at kseg0
  0x8804_0000, kstart first, .bss zeroed by kstart.
- src/arch/mips64: CP0 access, kstart building KernelArgs from linker symbols
  and MEMCFG0/1, Z85C30 serial console on IOC2 channel B, exception vectors
  copied to 0x8000_0000/0x80/0x180 (RAM through the low alias), a 38-word
  64-bit trap frame, software TLB refill from the rmm table, Count/Compare
  timer at 100 Hz, single-CPU percpu through a static pointer, context switch.
- rmm/src/arch/mips.rs: two-level 4-byte page tables, EntryLo-shaped leaves
  with software bits for user, no-execute and uncached, one ASID, flush on
  table switch.
- syscall/src/arch/mips64.rs: number in $v0, args $a0..$a5, result in $v0,
  thread pointer in $gp.
- panic.rs: no symbol lookup when no ELF header is loaded at KERNEL_OFFSET.
- Makefile: ARCH=mips64 uses llvm-objcopy and --no-default-features.

Measured on iris (indy_ip24, 32 MiB): kernel image 1036 KiB (text 896 KiB,
data 56 KiB, bss 84 KiB), TFTP file 975,056 bytes, 2052 KiB permanently
used after init_mm, 28,392 KiB (7098 frames) free with the 1 MiB heap mapped.

Signed-off-by: belikh <io@jupiter.au>
Signed-off-by: belikh <io@belic.net>
